HST Office on macOS: the ODF and OpenOffice.org types keep LSHandlerRank Owner (owner decision 2026-11-06).

hst-macos-coexist.patch lowered them to Default so an installed LibreOffice stays their default;
the owner prefers that a Mac with only HST opens .odt with HST (TextEdit took it at Default). The
types stay imported, not exported; with both suites installed LaunchServices picks one of the two
Owners and the other stays under Open With.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).

--- a/sysui/desktop/macosx/Info.plist.in
+++ b/sysui/desktop/macosx/Info.plist.in
@@ -23,7 +23,8 @@
     <string>English</string>
     <!-- HST Office imports every type it opens: the ODF, OpenOffice.org and extension types belong to
          their own suites (LibreOffice exports them), so a second export would make two conflicting
-         declarations of one type when both suites are installed. -->
+         declarations of one type when both suites are installed. HST still opens them as their Owner
+         (CFBundleDocumentTypes below), so a Mac with only HST opens them with HST. -->
     <key>UTImportedTypeDeclarations</key>
     <array>
         <!-- Writer documents -->
@@ -1569,8 +1570,6 @@
